@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}
<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white sm:text-4xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">Last updated: August 12, 2026</p>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-8 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
        <p>This policy explains what information Vistaways Tech ("we", "us") collects
            through ExamPortal, our candidate recruitment and assessment platform, and how
            we use it. It applies to candidates, and to Recruiter, HR, and Admin users of
            the platform. Vistaways Tech is based in Hyderabad, Telangana, India, and
            processes personal data as a "Data Fiduciary" under India's Digital Personal
            Data Protection Act, 2023 ("DPDP Act").</p>

        <section>
            <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">1. Information we collect</h2>
            <p class="mt-2">When you register and complete your profile, we collect: your
                full name, email address, mobile number, date of birth, gender, postal
                address, education history (college/university, degree, branch, graduation
                year), skills, a profile photo, your resume file, language proficiencies, and
                preferred job locations. If you sign in with Google instead of
                creating a password, we receive the account identifier, name, email, and
                profile picture Google shares with us, and nothing else from that
                account. As you move through the recruitment pipeline, we also record
                assessment results, interview records, and offer letter details tied to
                your application.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">2. Legal basis for processing</h2>
            <p class="mt-2">We process your personal data on the basis of your consent,
                given when you register an account and again where indicated at each
                subsequent step (for example, uploading a document or connecting a
                Google account). You may withdraw consent at any time by
                contacting us using the details below, though this may mean we can no
                longer consider you for a role, since we can't evaluate a candidacy
                without the underlying application data.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">3. How we use it</h2>
            <p class="mt-2">We use this information to evaluate your candidacy, schedule and
                run assessments and interviews, generate and issue offer letters, and
                communicate with you about the status of your application. We do not use
                your information for advertising, and we do not sell it.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">4. Who can see it</h2>
            <p class="mt-2">Your profile and application data is visible internally to
                Recruiter, HR, and Admin users involved in your hiring process. We do not
                share it with any organization outside Vistaways Tech, except where required
                by law.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">5. Data retention</h2>
            <p class="mt-2">We retain candidate records for as long as needed to consider you
                for current and future roles, and as required for our own record-keeping. If
                you'd like your data removed sooner, contact us using the details below and
                we'll act on that request.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">6. Cookies</h2>
            <p class="mt-2">See our <a asp-action="CookiePolicy" class="font-semibold text-[var(--vw-accent)] hover:underline">Cookie Policy</a> for the specific cookies this site sets — all of them are functional (keeping you signed in), none are used for advertising or tracking.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">7. Your rights</h2>
            <p class="mt-2">As a data principal under the DPDP Act, you have the right to:
                access a summary of the personal data we hold about you and how it's been
                processed; request correction or completion of inaccurate or incomplete
                data; request erasure of data that's no longer needed for the purpose it
                was collected for; withdraw consent (see section 2); nominate another
                individual to exercise these rights on your behalf in the event of your
                death or incapacity; and register a grievance with us, and — if unresolved
                — with the Data Protection Board of India. You can exercise any of these by
                contacting us using the details below.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">8. Contact &amp; grievance redressal</h2>
            <p class="mt-2">Questions about this policy, requests regarding your data, or
                grievances under the DPDP Act can be sent via our <a asp-action="ContactUs" class="font-semibold text-[var(--vw-accent)] hover:underline">Contact Us</a> page or to <a href="mailto:info@vistawaystech.com" class="font-semibold text-[var(--vw-accent)] hover:underline">info@vistawaystech.com</a>. A named Grievance Officer, as contemplated by the DPDP Act, should be designated here before this policy is relied on in production.</p>
        </section>

        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 dark:text-slate-500">This policy describes our actual data practices as implemented in ExamPortal, including a good-faith summary of DPDP Act concepts. It hasn't been reviewed by a lawyer — have it checked, and have a Grievance Officer formally designated (section 8), before relying on it as your sole compliance document.</p>
    </div>
</div>
